ART Bay Area Sea Level Rise and Shoreline Analysis Maps (AECOM 2017 for BCDC/MTC), Alameda County geodatabase Alameda_SLR_ART_2017.gdb.zip (5315663176 bytes).
Source: https://explorer.adaptingtorisingtides.org/download.php, POST r=prep&f=Alameda_gdb then r=fetch, HTTP Range requests for the zip directory and the Alameda_inundation_poly_<N> tables only.
Retrieved 2026-11-04T02:58:20Z. Rings whose bounding box meets the terrain grid plus 50 m are kept, coordinates EPSG:26910 rounded to 0.1 m.
Layer meaning: ART's connected flooding (inundated area hydraulically connected to the Bay), one feature per depth class (DEPTH_FT, feet), from the same ART study as the Caltrans service CHhqenvi/DEA_BCDC_polygon_SLR, which serves seven of the ten levels and differs from these polygons in detail (SOURCE_NOTES H5, C1).
